# --- Credentials: none exist in this repo today. These rules are preventive. ---
# Drive access currently runs through the claude.ai MCP connector (server-side OAuth),
# so there is no local client_secret/token file. If a future pipeline ever uses a
# local Google API client, its secrets land here and MUST stay untracked.
*.env
.env*
client_secret*.json
credentials*.json
token*.json
service-account*.json
service_account*.json
*oauth*.json
.netrc
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
*.keychain*

# --- Local tool/editor state ---
.claude/settings.local.json
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/

# --- OS ---
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db

# --- Incidental artifacts, not project sources ---
# A dump of a Claude Code terminal session. Scanned clean of secrets, but it is a
# conversation transcript rather than a build input -- excluded from a PUBLIC repo
# by default. Delete this line if you want it tracked.
full terminal convo.pdf

# --- Local caches / scratch (pipeline byproducts, not history) ---
.cache/
cache/
*.log
*.tmp
scratch/

# --- Build artifacts: pure functions of data/raw/ plus the scripts, which git
# already versions. Rebuild with `python3 scripts/build_dataset.py`.
# History is data/raw/ -- that is the part that cannot be regenerated (the
# rankings endpoint has no season pin, so a past season's official RPI table is
# gone once the season rolls over). Store raw, derive everything else.
data/data_2025.json
data/snapshots/
data/rpi_2025.json
data/bakeoff_2025.json

data/data_*.json
data/rating_*.json
data/bakeoff_*.json
data/rpi_2*.json

# Per-game player lines. For FINISHED seasons this is a resumable working file
# and only the aggregate is committed -- /boxscore is ID-addressed, so it can be
# re-crawled at will.
#
# THE LIVE SEASON IS DIFFERENT, and this is a correction paid for in a failed
# job. "Re-crawlable" turned out to carry an asterisk: a 2024 backfill ran fine
# for ~10k requests and then the API began hanging on every second one, leaving
# that season stuck at 43% and all of it August-September. Whatever that was,
# it means data you decline to take today may not be gettable later.
#
# The daily pipeline also runs on a FRESH CHECKOUT every morning. If this file
# is ignored, CI has nothing to resume from: it would refetch the whole season
# each day and throw the result away at the end of the job.
#
# So the live season's rows are committed. They arrive append-only at a few
# kilobytes a match, and they are what availability and next year's returning
# production are built from.
data/raw/2024/playerbox.jsonl
data/raw/2025/playerbox.jsonl

# Saved VolleyTalk pages (PDF / HTML / webarchive). Kept on disk, out of the
# PUBLIC repo on purpose: they contain forum members' posts, usernames and
# avatars, and committing them here would republish other people's writing.
# They are also redundant -- the anonymous live fetch is byte-identical to a
# logged-in save (measured, docs/data_sources.md §3), so nothing is preserved
# by keeping them under version control.
*Volley Talk*.pdf
*Volley Talk*.html
*Volley Talk*.webarchive

# Cody's personal quick-reference hub. Generated by scripts/build_cody_hub.py
# and read by nobody -- deleting it cannot affect a build. Kept out of this
# PUBLIC repo because Cody/data/tv_listings_2026.txt is transcribed from a
# VolleyTalk thread (same reasoning as the saved forum pages above).
Cody/

# The prediction log is the one file here that CANNOT be rebuilt: it records what
# the model said before each match was played, and re-deriving it afterwards from
# data that includes the outcome would be a fit, not a forecast. Committed.
!data/raw/2026/prediction_log.jsonl
